---
import Profile from '../layouts/Profile.astro';
import WorkstationMedia from '../components/WorkstationMedia.astro';
import '../styles/workstation.css';
---
<Profile title="Dave Bettner — Financial systems consulting" page="home" footerMessage={{title: 'Let’s talk about the work.', body: 'I’m interested in roles that bring accounting knowledge, technical consulting, and customer or partner enablement together.'}}>
  <section class="hero wrap">
    <div>
      <h1>Dave Bettner</h1>
      <h2>I make financial systems work in the real world.</h2>
      <p class="lede">I lead customer-facing implementations across reporting, integrations, training, and go-live—bringing accounting context and hands-on technical delivery to the work.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button" href="#selected-work">Explore my work</a>
        <a href="/dave-bettner-resume.pdf" download>Download résumé</a>
        <a href="mailto:dbett4@gmail.com">Get in touch</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="scene-wrap"><WorkstationMedia /></div>
  </section>
  <div class="proof wrap">
    <span>Workiva · Citrin Cooperman · LSL</span>
    <span>Accounting, technology, and customer delivery since 2015.</span>
    <span>Des Moines, Iowa</span>
  </div>
  <section class="section experience wrap">
    <div class="section-grid">
      <h2>I’ve worked on both sides of an implementation.</h2>
      <div>
        <p>At Workiva, I helped customers put the platform into use. At accounting firms, I’ve led the teams delivering it.</p>
        <p>That means working through the requirements with finance and IT, explaining the solution, training the people who will use it, and staying through testing and go-live.</p>
        <a class="section-link" href="/experience/">Explore my experience</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="selected-work" class="section wrap">
    <div class="section-grid">
      <h2>Connecting data collection and reporting.</h2>
      <div>
        <p>At Citrin Cooperman, I led a Workiva implementation connecting a customer’s system of record with its data-collection and reporting workflow.</p>
        <a class="section-link" href="/experience/connected-reporting/">Read the engagement summary</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="case">
      <div>
        <h3>Two systems, one workflow</h3>
        <p>Bidirectional API integration between Workiva and the customer’s system of record.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="facts">
        <div class="fact"><strong>Access and traceability</strong>Single sign-on and an audit trail within the implementation.</div>
        <div class="fact"><strong>Acceptance through launch</strong>Delivery leadership spanning user acceptance testing, go-live, and executive sign-off.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section wrap">
    <h2>What I’m building.</h2>
    <p class="project-intro">Alongside consulting, I build tools to explore where AI can help with accounting—and where it needs checks.</p>
    <div class="projects">
      <article class="project">
        <div>
          <h3><a href="/work/accounting-acceptance-lab/">Accounting Acceptance Lab</a></h3>
          <p>A Python and SQLite lab for testing accounting agents on reconciliation cases. It checks supporting evidence, approval requirements, and recovery from failed writes.</p>
          <p>Personal project. Synthetic cases, not client records.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <a href="/work/accounting-acceptance-lab/" aria-label="About the project: Accounting Acceptance Lab">About the project</a> ·
          <a href="https://github.com/dbett4/accounting-acceptance-lab" aria-label="View repository: Accounting Acceptance Lab">View repository</a>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="project">
        <div>
          <h3><a href="/work/regulated-reporting-mcp/">Regulated Reporting MCP</a></h3>
          <p>An MCP server that connects AI agents to reporting APIs through OAuth. It checks approval before writes and reads the result back to verify the change.</p>
          <p>Personal project. The public demo uses mock data.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <a href="/work/regulated-reporting-mcp/" aria-label="About the project: Regulated Reporting MCP">About the project</a> ·
          <a href="https://github.com/dbett4/regulated-reporting-mcp" aria-label="View repository: Regulated Reporting MCP">View repository</a>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
    <a class="section-link" href="/work/">More technical work</a>
  </section>
</Profile>
